    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pairs\n\n### Description\n\nCurrently neighbor patterns are used in `string.find`, which behaves correctly when the neighbors are indeed two bytes. But `strcharpart` respects multibyte characters, while `string.find` does not, resulting in misalignment.\n\nFor example, if I use a curly quote `“it|”` where bar indicates cursor, the neighbor pattern `[^%a].` of `'` will not prevent it from expanding to `“it'|'”`.",
    "closed_at": "2026-01-21T09:22:52Z",
