            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> * The [documentation](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/c163117900c17d4abf30bc09452a261c8536060c/doc/mini-pairs.txt#L169) should mention \"multibyte characters\".\n> \n> * Default patterns might be more useful. All of them are in the form of \"if left character is not ...\", so the can be translated into `^[^...]` form to be more multibyte friendly. The slight problem here is that it doesn't showcase the idea of \"it matches against exactly two characters\".\n\nBoth of these should now should be resolved on latest `main`. The default config should now work with the use case from the initial comment.",
